  "question": {
    "text": "A point charge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#181;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> is placed at the origin. At what location on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>-axis should a point charge of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#181;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> be placed so that the net electric field is zero at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math>-axis ?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0097_5fd6454d8bce.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 139px;\" /></p><p>Let the charge&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;C</mi></math>&nbsp;be placed at a distance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;from the origin&nbsp;as shown in the figure.</p><p>For the electric field at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>Therefore, the charge is located at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p>"
  }
}